{
  "id": "Compound::DB00910 - Gene::1576",
  "verbalization": "Paricalcitol, a vitamin D analog, is implicated in the regulation of steroid hormone metabolism through its interaction with Cyp24a1 and Cyp3a4. The evidence suggests that Paricalcitol binds to Cyp24a1, which then participates in monooxygenase activity, ultimately leading to the activation of Cyp3a4. This pathway highlights a direct interaction between Paricalcitol and Cyp3a4, mediated through Cyp24a1. Additionally, the presence of Paricalcitol in the same pathway as Calcitriol, which binds to Cyp3a4, further supports a role for Paricalcitol in modulating Cyp3a4 activity. The integration of these pathways underscores a mechanism by which Paricalcitol may influence Cyp3a4 through its effects on steroid hormone metabolism, potentially impacting drug metabolism and efficacy.",
